<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $158.1 mln Jan 23.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $158.1 mln Jan 23.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $158.1 million deficit on Jan 23 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JANUARY 23</p>
<p>Exports: $104.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $270.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $150.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $142 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $158.1 million</p>
<p>JANUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.440 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.751 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.176 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.945 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $920 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418))</p>
</text>
